# Copilot Rule: Image Insertion in Markdown

Whenever I request to add an image to a Markdown (.md) file, always use the following HTML snippet format:

<p>
    <img class="img-<choiceFromPrompt> snes-container no-padding" src="/images/<fileNameIGiveYou>">
</p>

Where:
- `<choiceFromPrompt>` is either `logo` or `game`, as specified in my prompt.
- `<fileNameIGiveYou>` is the image filename I provide as the source path.

Do not use Markdown image syntax (`![]()`), always use the HTML snippet above.

Example:
If I say: "Add a logo image wolfensteinNewOrder-logo.png", you should insert:

<p>
    <img class="img-logo snes-container no-padding" src="/images/wolfensteinNewOrder-logo.png">
</p>

If I say: "Add a game image doom-img1.jpg", you should insert:

<p>
    <img class="img-game snes-container no-padding" src="/images/doom-img1.jpg">
</p>
